mode: "100644"
text: "# The LADDER framework — LinkedIn growth is a system, not a posting habit\n\nLinkedIn rewards **dwell time and meaningful comments** on **personal profiles**, and its posts have\na long shelf life — so growth comes from a small number of strong posts, a daily commenting practice\non target accounts, and a profile that converts the resulting visits. LADDER is the 2026 engine.\n\n## L — Landing-page profile\nEvery post's job ends at a **profile visit**; the profile converts it or wastes it.\n- **Headline = value proposition** (\"I help X do Y\" / the specific expertise), not a job title —\n  it follows you into every comment you leave.\n- **About** opens with the ~3 lines visible before the fold; **Featured** holds the one CTA\n  (lead magnet, newsletter, site → `link-in-bio-and-traffic`).\n- **Follow-primary** once inbound outpaces outbound connecting. Craft → `profile-optimization`;\n  keywords → `social-seo`.\n\n## A — Author for dwell\n- 3–5 posts/week, **max 1/day**. Win the \"…see more\" tap (~140 chars), format for the phone read,\n  close on a genuine question. Craft → `linkedin-post-writer`, `hook-writer`.\n- Format mix by job: **document carousels** (authority + saves), **native video** (the 2026 push),\n  **text** (POV/story), occasional poll. **Link in the first comment, never the body.**\n- **Topic consistency** — the algorithm must be able to classify what you're the person for.\n\n## D — Deploy strategic comments (the afterburner)\n- Pick **10–20 target accounts**: bigger voices in the niche + peers + dream clients' feeds.\n- Leave **5–10 substantive comments/day** — add a data point, a counterpoint, a lived example;\n  never \"Great post!\". Your headline travels with every comment into *their* audience.\n- Comment early on fresh posts from large accounts. Drafts → `reply-and-comment-writer`; the daily\n  block → `engagement-routine`. A human posts them — no automation.\n\n## D — Drive the golden hour\n- The first **60–90 minutes** decide initial distribution. Post in the audience's window (weekday\n  working hours for most B2B — treat as guidance, not analytics).\n- **Reply to every comment** in that window, with replies that reopen the thread (end on a\n  question). Be active commenting 15 min before and after your own post — warm accounts get warmer\n  starts.\n\n## E — Expand with native surfaces\n- **Newsletter** — the notification + email push makes it the best owned-audience feature; launch\n  when you have a repeatable theme and ~1k+ followers (pairs with `email-and-newsletter`).\n- **Native video** weekly if capacity allows (→ `talking-head-and-piece-to-camera`); **audio\n  events** for warm-audience depth. Skip collaborative-article badge-chasing.\n- Check **SSI** monthly as a directional gauge — never optimize for the number.\n\n## R — Relationships & network hygiene\n- **Connections** (30k cap, ~100 invites/week) = the two-way network; **followers** (unlimited) =\n  the audience. Grow followers with content; spend invites on people you've already engaged.\n- Invite hygiene: comment first, connect second; short specific note when context isn't obvious;\n  **no pitch in the request**; withdraw stale invites.\n- DMs continue conversations that already started (→ `social-selling-and-dm`) — a pitch-slap after\n  an accept undoes the whole system.\n\n## The LinkedIn-growth brief a request should fill\n```\nFIT: is LinkedIn a priority (B2B, services, hiring, thought leadership)? Person, not page.\nPROFILE: headline = value prop; Featured = CTA; Follow-primary decision made\nPOSTS: 3-5/week, max 1/day; format mix (text / carousel / video / newsletter); link in first comment\nCOMMENTS: 10-20 target accounts; 5-10 substantive comments/day, drafted by agent, posted by human\nGOLDEN HOUR: audience window; reply to every comment in 60-90 min\nNETWORK: invite hygiene (no pitch, ~100/week); newsletter yes/no; SSI directional only\n```\n"
